<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulag</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1930">1930</a>–<a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gulag was the Soviet system of forced labour camps, named from the acronym of its Main Camps Administration, set up in 1930. Millions of people, many of them political prisoners, were held in camps across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, the far north and Kazakhstan, where they worked on mines, canals and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a>. The system was largely dismantled after Stalin's death in 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulag.jpg" alt="Gulag" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gulag_Location_Map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
